spec gg05-delete-everything-vs-insert: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# GG05. s1 runs MATCH (n) DETACH DELETE n; s2 creates a new node. s1's snapshot
# predates s2's commit in every order, so s1 cannot see the new node and it survives:
# a phantom insert is permitted, and a delete never reaches across snapshots.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2n s2c
step s1d: MATCH (n) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
3      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2n: CREATE (n:N {name:'new'}) RETURN n.name AS name
name 
-----
"new"
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name 
-----
"new"
(1 row)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
